            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/evidence.go: ResultRef accepts a ref only after it is cut into exactly \u003cResultsDir\u003e/\u003cfeature\u003e/\u003cname\u003e, with no extra slash. It then validates both segments with CheckFeature and CheckResultName before returning them, so absolute paths, dot-dot segments and nested paths are refused by shape before any file is read. The tests in engine/review/evidence_test.go cover traversal, absolute, backslash, trailing-slash, hidden-feature, temp-file, verdict-name and NUL-suffix refs.",
              "engine/review/evidence.go: VerdictRef compares the ref for exact equality with the path derived from the result via ResultPath and VerdictName. No arbitrary ref can name a verdict, and the result file itself is refused.",
              "engine/review/evidence.go: CheckFile and CheckRange compare public digests and refs, not secrets, so there is no timing or secret exposure. Error messages contain only the kind, ref and digests, which are not sensitive.",
              "The candidate is pure validation code with no file I/O, command execution, new dependencies or secrets. I found no reachable exploit introduced by this change. The behavior of CheckFeature and CheckResultName is outside the candidate, so I treated it as given."
            ]
          }
        }
