            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/evidence.go: ResultRef refuses by shape before any file is read. It rejects a ref without the results-directory prefix, a ref without exactly two segments after it, and a name that contains a slash, and it returns empty values on every refusal path. The feature and name rules are delegated to CheckFeature and CheckResultName, and their errors stay readable through errors.Is.",
              "engine/review/evidence.go: OptionalEvidence and RequiredEvidence handle the absent, single and repeated cases deterministically. The repeated case wraps ErrEvidenceRepeated, and the missing case wraps ErrEvidenceMissing.",
              "engine/review/evidence.go: VerdictRef compares the whole ref with the single path derived from the result name, so the result file itself, other results and traversal-shaped refs are all refused.",
              "engine/review/evidence.go: CheckFile and CheckRange fail closed, since the digest, base, head and range shape must match exactly. A zero Binding yields the range \"..\", which no real ref matches.",
              "engine/review/evidence_test.go: the tests assert observable results. They check the error sentinel, the EvidenceError Kind and Ref fields, the message content, empty returns on refusal, and the acceptance path for each function. Coverage includes many malformed-ref cases, a wrong-case payload kind, an interrupted review, repeated evidence, and range variants. The fixtures (candidate, storedRef, verdictRef and the SHA constants) are not visible in this candidate. I treated them as pre-existing and found no behavior left unproved by what is shown."
            ]
          }
